  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Never polls",
      "items": [
        "File changes arrive from inotify and git's fsmonitor daemon, debounced, and refresh only what changed",
        "The watcher stops at what git ignores: 765 watches for nine repositories, not 54,010",
        "Idle with nine repositories open: 0 % CPU"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Your git does the work",
      "items": [
        "Every write shells out to the git on your PATH, so hooks, signing, credential helpers and LFS behave as in your terminal",
        "One writing command at a time per repository; reads never wait",
        "Interactive rebase is planned in the UI and handed to git as its own todo file"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Keyboard first",
      "items": [
        "One command catalog drives the palette, the key strip and the settings",
        "Every list is virtualized, so 200k commits cost what 20 do",
        "The window shows in half a second; a keystroke that closes a dialog cannot reach the list behind it"
      ]
    }
  ]
